      "text": "Given the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\) with roots \\(r, s, t\\), we want to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\).\n\nFirst, expand the expression \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\):\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst + rst + srst\n\\]\n\nWe simplify this as follows:\n\n\\[\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + (rst - rst) + rst + rst\n\\]\n\nNotice that \\(rst - rst\\) simplifies to 0, so the expression further simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n1 + (r+s+t) + (rs+rt+st) + 2rst\n\\]\n\nBy Vieta's formulas, for the polynomial \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\):\n\n- The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = 20\\)\n- The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = 18\\)\n- The product of the roots \\(rst = 7\\)\n\nSubstituting these into our expression, we get:\n\n\\[\n1 + 20 + 18 + 2 \\times 7\n\\]\n\nCalculating the values inside the expression:\n\n\\[\n1 + 20 = 21\n\\]\n\\[\n21 + 18 = 39\n\\]\n\\[\n39 + 2 \\times 7 = 39 + 14 = 53\n\\]\n\nThus, the value is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{53}\n\\]",
